# Cybernetics — NestJS Application Design

> Status: **Approved design** for the initial scaffold. Implementation follows this document.
> Stack: NestJS 11 · Node 24 · pnpm 10 · TypeScript · **SWC** compiler.

## 1. Overview & Goals

Cybernetics is a modular NestJS 11 backend. This design establishes a clean, layered foundation with a
complete **infrastructure layer** (database, cache, logging, health, queues, observability), a **feature
layer** scaffolded for Mastra AI, and an empty **application layer** for future use-case/orchestration
modules. The project is built and tested with the **SWC** compiler for fast builds, with `tsc --noEmit`
retained for type safety.

Design principles: one cohesive `@Module` per infrastructure concern (sub-concerns are folders/providers,
not micro-modules); strongly-typed config via `@nestjs/config` + **Zod**; runtime DI decoupled from
CLI-time concerns (migrations/seeders); load-bearing bootstrap ordering documented explicitly.

